    "/apis/v1/earthquake-usgs-gov/earthquakes/search": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Find earthquakes (or other seismic events) in a time window, region or magnitude range: recent significant quakes, a historical sequence, quakes near a site. Use event for one event's ShakeMap, PAGER and DYFI summaries.\n\n<!-- aisa-pricing:start -->\nUsage-based billing; Default request estimate: $0.0005 USD (not a fixed price). Declared unit rate: $0.0001 USD per provider_credit. Account-specific pricing and final settlement may differ.\n<!-- aisa-pricing:end -->",
        "operationId": "earthquake-usgs-gov.earthquakes.search",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": false,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "properties": {
                  "alert_level": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Only events with this PAGER alert level.\n\nProvider reference: allowed values [\"green\", \"yellow\", \"orange\", \"red\"].",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "oneOf": [
                        "green",
                        "yellow",
                        "orange",
                        "red"
                      ]
                    }
                  },
                  "cursor": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "next_cursor from the previous page of the same search. Pattern: ^[0-9]{1,5}$.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body"
                    }
                  },
                  "end_time": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Latest origin time (inclusive), UTC, same formats. A bare date means 00:00:00 of that day. Defaults to now. Pattern: ^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}(T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}(:[0-9]{2}(\\.[0-9]{1,3})?)?)?Z?$.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body"
                    }
                  },
                  "event_type": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "ComCat event type, e.g. earthquake, explosion, quarry blast. Defaults to every type. Pattern: ^[a-z][a-z ]{0,39}$.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body"
                    }
                  },
                  "latitude": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Circle center latitude; requires longitude and max_radius_km.\n\nProvider reference: minimum -90; maximum 90.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": -90,
                      "max": 90
                    }
                  },
                  "limit": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Events per page.\n\nProvider reference: minimum 1; maximum 200; default 50.",
                    "default": 50,
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": 1,
                      "max": 200
                    }
                  },
                  "longitude": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Circle center longitude.\n\nProvider reference: minimum -180; maximum 180.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": -180,
                      "max": 180
                    }
                  },
                  "max_depth_km": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "max_depth_km\n\nProvider reference: minimum -100; maximum 1000.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": -100,
                      "max": 1000
                    }
                  },
                  "max_latitude": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Rectangle north edge.\n\nProvider reference: minimum -90; maximum 90.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": -90,
                      "max": 90
                    }
                  },
                  "max_longitude": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Rectangle east edge.\n\nProvider reference: minimum -360; maximum 360.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": -360,
                      "max": 360
                    }
                  },
                  "max_magnitude": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "max_magnitude\n\nProvider reference: minimum -2; maximum 10.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": -2,
                      "max": 10
                    }
                  },
                  "max_radius_km": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Circle radius in kilometres.\n\nProvider reference: minimum 0; maximum 20001.6.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": 0,
                      "max": 20001.6
                    }
                  },
                  "min_depth_km": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "min_depth_km\n\nProvider reference: minimum -100; maximum 1000.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": -100,
                      "max": 1000
                    }
                  },
                  "min_latitude": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Rectangle south edge. Rectangle edges may be given in any subset; do not combine with the circle.\n\nProvider reference: minimum -90; maximum 90.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": -90,
                      "max": 90
                    }
                  },
                  "min_longitude": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Rectangle west edge; values beyond +/-180 let a rectangle cross the antimeridian.\n\nProvider reference: minimum -360; maximum 360.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": -360,
                      "max": 360
                    }
                  },
                  "min_magnitude": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "min_magnitude\n\nProvider reference: minimum -2; maximum 10.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": -2,
                      "max": 10
                    }
                  },
                  "order_by": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Newest first (time), oldest first, largest first (magnitude) or smallest first.\n\nProvider reference: allowed values [\"time\", \"time-asc\", \"magnitude\", \"magnitude-asc\"]; default \"time\".",
                    "default": "time",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "oneOf": [
                        "time",
                        "time-asc",
                        "magnitude",
                        "magnitude-asc"
                      ]
                    }
                  },
                  "start_time": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Earliest origin time, UTC: YYYY-MM-DD or YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM[:SS[.fff]][Z]. Defaults to 30 days ago. Pattern: ^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}(T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}(:[0-9]{2}(\\.[0-9]{1,3})?)?)?Z?$.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body"
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              "examples": {
                "provider": {
                  "summary": "Official provider example; checked against AIsa request constraints",
                  "value": {
                    "end_time": "2011-03-12",
                    "limit": 5,
                    "min_magnitude": 7,
                    "order_by": "magnitude",
                    "start_time": "2011-03-11"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Search the USGS ComCat earthquake catalog through the FDSN event web service (/fdsnws/event/1/query, GeoJSON) by origin-time window, magnitude and depth ranges, a latitude/longitude rectangle or a point plus radius, PAGER alert level and event type. Returns normalized events (ISO-8601 UTC times, latitude/longitude/depth_km, preferred magnitude and type, place, PAGER alert, tsunami flag, DYFI felt reports and intensities, significance, review status, event page URL). Pages with cursor/next_cursor (FDSN offset). Without start_time USGS searches the last 30 days; without end_time it searches up to now.\n\nThe response contains the tool result directly.\n\nThe provider identifies `events` as the primary payload key.\n\n| Documented field | Provider type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `alert` | string | PAGER alert level; null when PAGER did not run or has not published. |\n| `azimuthal_gap_deg` | number | Largest azimuthal gap between stations, degrees. |\n| `cdi` | number | Maximum reported (DYFI) intensity, Modified Mercalli scale. |\n| `code` | string | Network-assigned event code. |\n| `depth_km` | number | Hypocenter depth in kilometres below sea level (negative above). |\n| `event_type` | string | earthquake, quarry blast, explosion, ice quake, ... |\n| `felt` | number | Number of Did You Feel It? reports; null when there are none. |\n| `id` | string | Preferred ComCat event id (network + code), e.g. us6000jllz. |\n| `ids` | string[] | Every id associated with this event, including ids contributed by other networks; any of them resolves to this event. |\n| `latitude` | number |  |\n| `longitude` | number |  |\n| `magnitude` | number | Preferred magnitude; null when ComCat has none. |\n| `magnitude_type` | string | Magnitude type of the preferred magnitude (mww, mb, ml, md, ...). |\n| `min_distance_deg` | number | Horizontal distance from the epicenter to the nearest station, degrees. |\n| `mmi` | number | Maximum estimated (ShakeMap) instrumental intensity, Modified Mercalli scale. |\n| `network` | string | Network that contributed the preferred solution (us, ci, ak, official, ...). |\n| `place` | string | Named region or distance-and-direction from the nearest place, as USGS publishes it (some non-ASCII names arrive as '?'). |\n| `product_types` | string[] | ComCat product types attached to the event (origin, shakemap, losspager, dyfi, moment-tensor, ...). |\n| `rms_s` | number | Root-mean-square travel-time residual, seconds. |\n| `significance` | number | USGS significance score (0 to ~3000) combining magnitude, felt reports and estimated impact. |\n| `sources` | string[] | Networks that contributed information. |\n| `stations` | number | Number of seismic stations used to locate the event. |\n| `status` | string | automatic (not yet reviewed by a seismologist) or reviewed. |\n| `time` | string | Origin time, ISO-8601 UTC. |\n| `title` | string | USGS display title, e.g. \"M 7.8 - Pazarcik earthquake, ...\". |\n| `tsunami` | boolean | True when the event is in an oceanic region that the tsunami warning centers may evaluate. It does not mean a tsunami occurred or a warning was issued. |\n| `updated` | string | When ComCat last updated the event (any product), ISO-8601 UTC. |\n| `url` | string | USGS event page. |\n\n\nThese are the provider's documented fields. Field requiredness, nullability and nested object structures are specified only where the descriptions explicitly say so.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "not": {
                    "type": "null"
                  },
                  "x-aisa-schema-completeness": "documented-fields-only"
                },
                "examples": {
